  en: {
    'skip':'Skip to content','nav.features':'Features','nav.providers':'Providers','nav.agents':'Agents','nav.download':'Download','nav.faq':'FAQ','nav.get':'Download','lang.label':'Language',
    'hero.badge':'Version 0.1.0 · Windows x64','hero.title':'Any model. Every tool. <em>Finished work.</em>',
    'hero.lead':'Cude is an AI code editor that plans, writes and verifies real changes in your project. Use the provider you choose, a local model on your PC, or the models inside the coding tools and editors you already have. Nothing runs without your approval.',
    'hero.download':'Download for Windows','hero.tour':'See how it works','hero.meta':'Free · One installer · Your API keys stay in Windows secure storage',
    'feat.kicker':'One window, the whole loop','feat.title':'From prompt to passing tests.','feat.sub':'A full Code-OSS editor with an agent that reads your project, edits files, runs your commands after you approve them and keeps an undo for every change.',
    'f1.t':'An agent that finishes','f1.p':'It reads files, edits code, runs your tests and fixes what fails, one step at a time, until the job is done.',
    'f2.t':'Cuets: a team of agents','f2.p':'A planner, parallel workers and a reviewer split big tasks and stop only when your project checks pass.',
    'f3.t':'Computer use and browser control','f3.p':'Cude sees windows, clicks and types in desktop apps and drives its own separate browser profile. Every action asks first; passwords, admin windows and your own browser are never touched.',
    'f4.t':'Every model you already have','f4.p':'65 ready-made connections, any OpenAI-compatible API, local GGUF models, and the models inside OpenCode, Codex, Claude Code, Gemini CLI and your other editors.',
    'f5.t':'Voice','f5.p':'Dictate with the microphone and hear answers in the Windows voice for your language. No extra installs.',
    'f6.t':'Safe by default','f6.p':'Keys live in OS secure storage; commands, tool calls and full access always ask first.',
    'f7.t':'A bridge for your desktop apps','f7.p':'Claude Desktop, Cursor, VS Code, Antigravity, OpenCode and other MCP apps can use Cude\'s project tools through its local bridge, with your approval in Cude.',
    'f9.t':'Android and 3D, built in','f9.p':'Build, install and debug Android apps from the + menu, and turn an image into a ready-to-run Three.js scene for your game.','f8.t':'Never left stuck','f8.p':'If a model runs out of quota or is retired, Cude switches to another connected model and tells you. A memory guard warns before your PC runs out of memory and frees space in one click.',
    'pr.kicker':'Your models, your rules','pr.title':'Bring any model. Switch in a click.','pr.sub':'Pick a provider, paste a key and Cude lists its models and reasoning levels. Local servers, coding CLIs and editor models have their own tabs, so setup stays clean.',
    'pr.local':'Local GGUF (llama.cpp)','pr.more':'+ any OpenAI-compatible API',
    'ag.kicker':'Agents that check their work','ag.title':'Hand off the whole task.','ag.sub':'Cuets breaks a request into a checklist, runs workers in parallel and verifies the result with your own test command before calling it done.',
    'ag.l1':'Long tasks are saved in the project and can be resumed','ag.l2':'Round and time budgets, so nothing runs forever','ag.l3':'Run Codex, Claude Code, OpenCode, Gemini CLI or Qwen Code as the engine, with any of their models',
    'dl.kicker':'Download','dl.title':'Start building in minutes.','dl.sub':'One installer. It installs into your user folder, so no administrator rights are needed.',
    'dl.req':'Windows 10 or 11 (64-bit) · 8 GB RAM recommended','dl.version':'Version','dl.size':'Size','dl.type':'Type','dl.button':'Download CudeIDE-Setup-0.1.0-x64.exe','dl.copy':'Copy','dl.copied':'Copied',
    'dl.how':'How to start','dl.s1':'Run the installer. If Windows SmartScreen appears, choose "More info" → "Run anyway".','dl.s2':'Cude IDE opens from the Start menu and your desktop.','dl.s3':'Open a project, trust the folder and connect a provider from the model menu.','dl.s4':'Optional: check the download in PowerShell',
    'faq.title':'Questions','q1':'Is Cude IDE free?','a1':'Yes. You pay only your model provider for usage on your own key; local models and local agents use their own resources.',
    'q2':'Where are my API keys stored?','a2':'In the Windows secure credential storage through the editor\'s secret storage. They are never written into project files or sent anywhere except the provider you chose.',
    'q3':'Can the agent change things without asking?','a3':'In Auto mode it writes file edits and keeps an undo. Terminal commands, MCP tool calls, computer and browser actions always ask first; Read-only and Plan modes never write.',
    'q7':'Can I use the models from my other AI tools and editors?','a7':'Yes. Cude finds OpenCode, Codex CLI, Claude Code, Gemini CLI and other coding tools on your PC and lists their models in its model menu. Desktop apps that speak MCP can connect to Cude in one click.',
    'q4':'Why does Windows show a warning?','a4':'The 0.1.0 installer is not code-signed yet, so SmartScreen may warn on first launch. You can confirm the file is intact with the SHA-256 value above.',
    'q5':'What is it built on?','a5':'Cude IDE is built on the open-source Code-OSS editor (via VSCodium) with Cude\'s own AI extension, theme and settings. The MIT license and third-party notices ship with the app.',
    'q6':'Mac or Linux?','a6':'Version 0.1.0 is Windows x64 only. Other platforms are planned.',
    'foot.note':'Code-OSS and VSCodium are MIT licensed. Cude is not affiliated with Microsoft.',
    'prod.alt':'Cude IDE agent working on a task next to the provider settings','pr.alt':'Cude IDE provider settings with grouped providers and logos','lo.alt':'Cude IDE first-run welcome and setup'
  },
